  "overview": {
    "title": "Lanes of earth and memory",
    "p1": "Amezrou (Amazrou) is the oasis village side of Zagora: narrow lanes, earthen walls and traces of the old Jewish quarter that once formed part of the town’s social fabric.",
    "p2": "It is best on foot. A short walk gives more sense of daily Draa life than the main road strip. Local guides sometimes offer context for a tip.",
    "p3": "Stay respectful in residential lanes and ask before photographing people or private doorways."
